   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the estates, powers and trusts law, in relation to allowing a\nduly appointed personal representative of the estate of a victim of the\nSeptember eleventh, two thousand one terrorist attacks to file a claim with\nthe September eleventh victim compensation fund",
    "basePrintNo": "S6812",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6812-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §11-4.7, EPT L",
    "lawSection": "Estates, Powers and Trusts Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6812\n\nSPONSOR: GOUNARDES\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the estates, powers and trusts law, in relation to\nallowing a duly appointed personal representative of the estate of a\nvictim of the September eleventh, two thousand one terrorist attacks to\nfile a claim with the September eleventh victim compensation fund\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe proposed legislation would treat the filing and processing by the\nVCF of a personal injury claim against the VCF of a victim who did not\ndie as a result of his/her injuries the same as a victim who had died as\na result of his/her injuries.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one of the bill amends section 11-4.7 of the Estates, Powers and\nTrusts Law relating to the liability of the personal representative of a\ndecedent receiving an award from the 9/11 Victims Compensation Fund.\n\nSection two sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nCurrently, the Surrogate's court routinely places restrictions on the\nletters issued to a personal representative as it pertains to the prose-\ncution, compromise and collection of any settlement under New York's\nwrongful death statute. A claim against the 9/11 VCF of a victim who\ndied as a result of his/her 9/11 injury can be filed and processed with-\nout additional invention of the Surrogate's Court despite these\nrestrictions because VCF is able to rely on EPTL 11-4.7e(3) which allows\nthe filing and processing of the claim despite the restrictions on the\npersonal representative's powers. Due to the language of EPTL 11-4.7e(3)\nwhich applies to a victim who dies as a result of his/her 9/11 injury, a\nclaim against the VCF of a victim who did not die as a result of his/her\n9/11 injury but still sustained a compensable injury is delayed until an\napplication is made to the Surrogate's Court for either amended letters\nor an order clarifying the restrictions on the letters as it pertains to\nthe filing of the VCF claim.\n\nThis bill seeks to treat all victims of the World Trade Center terrorist\nattack and the processing of their claims equally without unnecessary\ndelay. It also seeks to minimize the administrative burden on the fami-\nly, VCF, and the Surrogate's Court by allowing personal representatives\nof 9/11 decedents to file and process claims regardless of whether the\ndecedent died of the 9/11 illness or simply sustained a 9/11 injury but\ndied of a different cause.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNone\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\n\n\nIf enacted, this proposed legislation would create administrative\nsavings in the VCF and the Surrogate's Court due to the elimination of\nan unnecessary step in the VCF claims process.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediate\n",
